00:19:08.744 --> 00:19:09.578
Right?

00:19:11.414 --> 00:19:14.517
You didn't have to bring these.

00:19:14.517 --> 00:19:18.287
She could've thanked us by buying coffee or getting her hair done here.

00:19:20.056 --> 00:19:21.524
So...

00:19:21.524 --> 00:19:23.592
Don't just stand there. Come have a seat.

00:19:23.592 --> 00:19:24.660
Okay.

00:19:26.562 --> 00:19:29.565
The hair salon is small...

00:19:30.533 --> 00:19:33.736
I mean, cozy and nice.

00:19:34.570 --> 00:19:37.740
And your hairstyle is...

00:19:37.740 --> 00:19:42.978
Retro styles like this are coming back in fashion these days.

00:19:42.978 --> 00:19:44.814
This is the latest style.

00:19:46.015 --> 00:19:49.785
Hye Sun is so good...

00:19:49.785 --> 00:19:51.354
that once she gives you a perm,

00:19:51.354 --> 00:19:53.823
it lasts at least a year.

00:19:53.823 --> 00:19:55.291
That's right.

00:19:55.291 --> 00:19:56.459
A perm...

00:19:56.459 --> 00:19:58.527
must last until Chuseok to get your money's worth.

00:19:58.527 --> 00:19:59.662
You're right.

00:20:00.563 --> 00:20:02.665
That's really practical.

00:20:04.133 --> 00:20:08.771
But if the rollers were a little thicker,

00:20:08.771 --> 00:20:11.574
it could look like that trendy hush perm style...

00:20:11.574 --> 00:20:14.410
that's popular with younger people.

00:20:14.410 --> 00:20:17.813
Right now, it's too flat on the head...

00:20:17.813 --> 00:20:20.950
so it brings out your head shape too honestly.

00:20:20.950 --> 00:20:22.918
It's too blatantly showing.

00:20:22.918 --> 00:20:25.354
It's curled a bit too tightly.

00:20:25.354 --> 00:20:26.122
Honestly?

00:20:27.023 --> 00:20:28.090
What has that got to do with her hairstyle?

00:20:30.359 --> 00:20:32.662
What I mean is...

00:20:32.662 --> 00:20:35.364
since you're so skilled,

00:20:35.364 --> 00:20:37.533
if the perm looked a little more natural,

00:20:37.533 --> 00:20:41.003
it could look a bit more elegant.

00:20:41.804 --> 00:20:43.305
Right now, it looks...

00:20:43.305 --> 00:20:46.442
like an old maid's style.

00:20:47.777 --> 00:20:49.879
Forget looking natural.

00:20:49.879 --> 00:20:53.849
Isn't it a good thing if a granny looks like an old maid?

00:20:54.617 --> 00:20:56.552
Where you come from,

00:20:56.952 --> 00:21:01.057
maybe looking natural seems elegant.

00:21:01.057 --> 00:21:03.459
But here, once you plant seedlings,

00:21:03.459 --> 00:21:05.761
your hair falls apart and you end up looking like a mountain god.

00:21:07.096 --> 00:21:08.264
Unbelievable.

00:21:08.497 --> 00:21:11.400
No, that's not what I meant.

00:21:11.400 --> 00:21:13.869
But once you are done...

00:21:13.869 --> 00:21:15.004
That's enough.

00:21:15.004 --> 00:21:16.005
I think she'd look elegant.

00:21:16.005 --> 00:21:16.839
Stop it.

00:21:24.547 --> 00:21:25.414
Ji Sang.

00:21:26.082 --> 00:21:28.317
Do you still want to go to Toronto?

00:21:28.317 --> 00:21:29.852
I don't know.

00:21:29.852 --> 00:21:31.053
I like here.

00:21:31.554 --> 00:21:34.156
The village chief next door is nice,

00:21:34.156 --> 00:21:36.058
and Bo Mi is always kind to us too.

00:21:36.726 --> 00:21:38.594
Everyone helped with finding us.

00:21:39.095 --> 00:21:41.430
I like going to Dad's field too.

00:21:43.766 --> 00:21:46.836
All I need is Carol.

00:21:47.903 --> 00:21:49.438
Carol.

00:21:49.872 --> 00:21:50.973
You were dumped.

00:21:53.976 --> 00:21:56.612
I can be dumped because I dated her.

00:21:57.947 --> 00:21:59.482
That's right.

00:21:59.482 --> 00:22:01.450
The one who's never dated, always gets rejected.

00:22:03.819 --> 00:22:06.055
Be quiet. I have dated before.

00:22:06.055 --> 00:22:07.923
I've been on a date...

00:22:09.258 --> 00:22:10.526
A date?

00:22:11.327 --> 00:22:12.395
With whom?

00:22:12.395 --> 00:22:13.329
Here, bro?

00:22:16.499 --> 00:22:17.833
Who's the expert on relationships?

00:22:18.801 --> 00:22:19.769
Me, Seong Ji Sang.

00:22:20.102 --> 00:22:21.137
Did you tell her how you feel?

00:22:21.604 --> 00:22:22.405
No, right?

00:22:23.172 --> 00:22:25.174
That's why you'll stay single forever.

00:22:26.208 --> 00:22:29.679
A man needs to be bold. Power, okay?

00:22:30.179 --> 00:22:31.213
Power.

00:22:34.984 --> 00:22:37.053
What are you saying? Just go to sleep.

00:22:37.053 --> 00:22:38.287
I'm serious.

00:22:44.927 --> 00:22:47.797
(Menu Lineup)

00:23:00.743 --> 00:23:03.679
Can we go to the apple orchard again sometime?

00:23:11.287 --> 00:23:13.723
There's something I want to tell you.

00:23:19.261 --> 00:23:20.262
I think...

00:23:21.130 --> 00:23:22.565
I'm starting to like it here more.

00:23:24.667 --> 00:23:26.502
I must've lost my mind.

00:23:48.991 --> 00:23:50.826
Let's see.

00:23:56.198 --> 00:23:57.166
It's too sweet.

00:23:58.067 --> 00:24:00.369
What do you mean? It's a dessert. It's perfect sweetness.

00:24:00.369 --> 00:24:02.605
No, it's too sweet. Your mom wouldn't like it.

00:24:02.605 --> 00:24:04.507
No, it's because it's at room temperature now.

00:24:04.507 --> 00:24:06.575
Mousse is supposed to be...

00:24:06.876 --> 00:24:08.911
eaten cold.

00:24:11.113 --> 00:24:12.048
Is it too sweet?

00:24:18.554 --> 00:24:21.090
True. Mom needs to stay healthy.

00:24:27.830 --> 00:24:29.432
(Seong Ji Cheon)

00:24:43.546 --> 00:24:44.847
Do you like sweets?

00:24:45.781 --> 00:24:48.317
I made some apple mousse. Would you like some?

00:24:59.962 --> 00:25:01.063
Hi, Ji Cheon.

00:25:01.931 --> 00:25:04.900
I texted the head cook,

00:25:04.900 --> 00:25:06.168
but she hasn't checked it.

00:25:06.502 --> 00:25:09.005
Yes, about switching kimchi to radish kimchi.

00:25:09.005 --> 00:25:09.872
Yes.

00:25:10.339 --> 00:25:12.575
That? I'll take it with me.

00:25:12.575 --> 00:25:13.442
I'm here now.

00:25:13.442 --> 00:25:14.243
Bo Mi.

00:25:17.446 --> 00:25:18.614
You're late, which is unusual.

00:25:20.316 --> 00:25:22.752
I couldn't sleep well last night.

00:25:24.954 --> 00:25:26.789
I'm running late, so I'll get going now.

00:25:26.789 --> 00:25:27.590
Okay.

00:25:27.590 --> 00:25:28.457
- Take care. - Goodbye.

00:25:38.567 --> 00:25:39.301
Bo...

00:25:53.015 --> 00:25:53.883
What's going on?

00:25:55.951 --> 00:25:58.154
He went through all that trouble, even collecting manure to grow them.

00:25:58.154 --> 00:25:59.488
So why did he take them inside?

00:26:01.824 --> 00:26:03.526
And why isn't he coming back out?

00:26:07.830 --> 00:26:09.265
Something feels off.

00:26:16.372 --> 00:26:21.344
(Seedling sample submission D-1)

00:26:27.483 --> 00:26:30.853
I'll plant the ones left in the nursery both inside and outside.

00:26:30.853 --> 00:26:33.889
These will be sent to headquarters.

00:26:33.889 --> 00:26:34.724
Okay.

00:26:49.171 --> 00:26:50.072
Bo Mi.

00:26:50.439 --> 00:26:52.041
What are you looking for?

00:26:52.441 --> 00:26:54.543
My USB.

00:26:54.910 --> 00:26:57.046
It has several months' worth of meal plans on it,

00:26:57.046 --> 00:26:58.848
but I can't find it.

00:26:58.848 --> 00:27:01.250
If it's months' worth of meal plans, isn't it important?

00:27:01.684 --> 00:27:02.952
Yes.

00:27:02.952 --> 00:27:05.521
I did stay up all night working on it.

00:27:06.355 --> 00:27:08.891
But it's okay. If I can't find it, I'll just stay up all night again.

00:27:14.997 --> 00:27:15.998
Hi, Officer Park.

00:27:17.366 --> 00:27:19.669
What? Yes. That's mine.

00:27:20.736 --> 00:27:22.738
I'll head to the front gate right now.

00:27:23.172 --> 00:27:24.073
Thank you.

00:27:24.774 --> 00:27:25.775
Officer Park?

00:27:26.876 --> 00:27:28.911
Officer Park said he found it and brought it over.

00:27:28.911 --> 00:27:30.112
- I see. - What a relief.

00:27:30.112 --> 00:27:31.781
- I'll go get it right now. - Okay.

00:27:33.249 --> 00:27:36.218
Officer Park scored some points there.

00:27:36.852 --> 00:27:38.821
But what's the point of looking after her like this?

00:27:39.121 --> 00:27:41.524
When is he going to tell her how he feels?

00:27:41.924 --> 00:27:42.892
Tell her how he feels?

00:27:43.259 --> 00:27:44.226
Why?

00:27:44.226 --> 00:27:46.395
Everyone in Yeonri-ri knows...

00:27:46.395 --> 00:27:48.497
that Officer Park likes Bo Mi.

00:27:59.275 --> 00:28:00.343
Officer Park.

00:28:01.577 --> 00:28:03.012
You didn't have to rush.

00:28:04.513 --> 00:28:07.316
You weren't reading my text, so I called.

00:28:07.316 --> 00:28:08.918
I thought it might be important.

00:28:08.918 --> 00:28:11.087
Yes, it's important. Thank you.

00:28:11.087 --> 00:28:12.688
Really? That's great news.

00:28:13.055 --> 00:28:14.757
You didn't have to give me this too.

00:28:14.757 --> 00:28:15.991
You're the best.

00:28:16.826 --> 00:28:18.494
- If you are grateful... - He...

00:28:18.494 --> 00:28:20.763
Why don't we grab a meal together?

00:28:22.498 --> 00:28:26.335
A man needs to be bold. Power, okay?

00:28:29.105 --> 00:28:30.740
I don't want to pressure you.

00:28:30.740 --> 00:28:32.274
Hello, Officer Park.

00:28:44.854 --> 00:28:47.356
Am I interrupting?

00:28:48.557 --> 00:28:49.558
A little.

00:28:50.626 --> 00:28:52.928
Ji Cheon, what are you doing out here?

00:28:53.396 --> 00:28:56.565
You ran out in a hurry...

00:28:56.565 --> 00:28:58.601
so I thought maybe I could help with something.

00:29:00.302 --> 00:29:02.405
Both of you, thank you. I feel reassured.

00:29:03.205 --> 00:29:05.508
Should we set a date to hang out sometime?

00:29:07.109 --> 00:29:08.244
Let me check my schedule.

00:29:08.611 --> 00:29:11.113
Okay. I'll wait to hear from you.

00:29:12.081 --> 00:29:13.416
- Thanks for this. - Sure.

00:29:14.116 --> 00:29:15.418
- Goodbye. - Goodbye.

00:29:18.454 --> 00:29:19.321
Bye.

00:29:27.863 --> 00:29:29.265
Have that meal with me.

00:29:29.999 --> 00:29:30.833
Okay.

00:29:31.133 --> 00:29:32.068
For real?

00:29:32.068 --> 00:29:33.569
Sure. Why not?

00:29:37.139 --> 00:29:37.940
Look at you.

00:29:39.141 --> 00:29:40.910
You're trying to make a move too, aren't you?

00:29:58.594 --> 00:29:59.996
Are you quitting farming?

00:30:00.629 --> 00:30:02.631
That's great news.

00:30:06.002 --> 00:30:06.936
Chief.

00:30:10.239 --> 00:30:13.342
When my kids were lost and when I was sick,

00:30:14.377 --> 00:30:15.378
thank you for helping us out.

00:30:16.679 --> 00:30:20.116
Thanks to you, I'm able to send seedling samples to headquarters.

00:30:22.918 --> 00:30:24.020
What did you just say?

00:30:26.555 --> 00:30:27.490
The seedling sam...

00:30:30.393 --> 00:30:33.429
You grew those cabbages with your sweat and tears.

00:30:33.896 --> 00:30:35.831
You want to hand them over to those people again?

00:30:36.532 --> 00:30:38.534
I told you.

00:30:38.901 --> 00:30:41.570
I came here to do research and development on cabbage for headquarters.

00:30:41.570 --> 00:30:42.805
Yes, that's great.

00:30:42.805 --> 00:30:45.041
It's already a miracle that you grew them this much.

00:30:45.374 --> 00:30:47.877
But it's too late in the season now. Even if you grow them, they won't thrive.

00:30:48.277 --> 00:30:50.780
Think about it, Mr. Seong.

00:30:51.480 --> 00:30:53.416
When you said you were going to farm here,

00:30:53.416 --> 00:30:54.984
why do you think I was against it?

00:30:55.618 --> 00:30:57.186
Because you were some crazy stranger?

00:31:01.924 --> 00:31:02.758
Chief.

00:31:05.061 --> 00:31:08.431
If there's a problem, please explain it properly.

00:31:08.431 --> 00:31:09.965
I'm going crazy here.

00:31:10.666 --> 00:31:14.136
Work and raising my kids... They are all just so hard.

00:31:14.603 --> 00:31:16.772
For over 20 years until I became a manager,

00:31:16.772 --> 00:31:19.342
I was at my desk doing research.

00:31:19.342 --> 00:31:20.643
Do you think I ever imagined...

00:31:20.643 --> 00:31:23.179
moving rocks and rolling around in manure...

00:31:23.179 --> 00:31:25.147
at this age?

00:31:27.216 --> 00:31:31.220
I don't care what I go through. I can endure anything.

00:31:31.921 --> 00:31:33.689
But not my family.

00:31:34.890 --> 00:31:37.460
I will get through this no matter what and go back.

00:31:37.460 --> 00:31:39.595
Back to my position at Mat Story in Seoul.

00:31:47.803 --> 00:31:49.005
Unbelievable.

00:31:51.540 --> 00:31:52.475
Air holes.

00:31:54.310 --> 00:31:55.111
What?

00:31:56.045 --> 00:31:57.880
Make air holes.

00:31:59.148 --> 00:32:02.385
Both you and the seedlings need air holes to breathe, right?

00:32:02.385 --> 00:32:03.452
And...

00:32:03.452 --> 00:32:05.788
What am I saying right now? Darn.

00:32:27.777 --> 00:32:28.844
Im Ju Hyeong.

00:32:29.111 --> 00:32:32.014
Did you or did you not tell us to sign here?

00:32:32.682 --> 00:32:35.117
You said we could farm and supply cabbage steadily...

00:32:35.117 --> 00:32:37.186
to a conglomerate.

00:32:37.186 --> 00:32:41.557
How are we supposed to make a living now?

00:32:41.557 --> 00:32:43.759
Fix this now.

00:32:43.759 --> 00:32:45.294
And you call yourself the village chief?

00:32:45.294 --> 00:32:46.929
Do you call yourself the village chief?

00:32:48.864 --> 00:32:50.733
(Village chief)

00:33:16.592 --> 00:33:17.860
It's making me uneasy.

00:33:39.648 --> 00:33:41.550
Chief. I'm making the air holes...

00:33:44.620 --> 00:33:45.521
Sir.

00:33:46.422 --> 00:33:47.656
The company is sending...

00:33:48.157 --> 00:33:50.226
a truck tomorrow to pick up the samples.

00:33:51.127 --> 00:33:53.796
No, I'll take them to Seoul myself.

00:33:53.796 --> 00:33:54.930
I can't let anything happen to them.

00:34:00.269 --> 00:34:03.472
You don't trust the company?

00:34:04.006 --> 00:34:05.174
I do.

00:34:05.174 --> 00:34:07.043
I'm the supplier so it's my responsibility.

00:34:07.043 --> 00:34:09.145
So it's right that I take them to Seoul myself.

00:34:11.947 --> 00:34:14.684
Suit yourself.

00:34:38.507 --> 00:34:40.076
How long do you have to stay here?

00:34:41.110 --> 00:34:43.846
What is it now? Did something happen?

00:34:44.580 --> 00:34:48.351
I really don't get along with the women in this town.

00:34:48.718 --> 00:34:50.319
Did I say something wrong?

00:34:51.053 --> 00:34:54.023
I said those things for their benefit.

00:34:54.023 --> 00:34:55.825
I meant well with everything I said.

00:34:56.959 --> 00:35:00.096
They just think differently from us. That's all.

00:35:00.096 --> 00:35:02.031
It's not...

00:35:03.532 --> 00:35:04.767
Why don't you take my side?

00:35:13.476 --> 00:35:14.343
Honey.

00:35:15.945 --> 00:35:18.748
What kind of father have I been to the kids?

00:35:21.951 --> 00:35:22.852
What do you mean?

00:35:23.819 --> 00:35:24.820
Why are you asking me that?

00:35:26.655 --> 00:35:28.024
Did Ji Cheon...

00:35:29.425 --> 00:35:32.261
ever say he wanted to be a doctor?

00:35:32.762 --> 00:35:35.631
What? Why are you asking such weird questions?

00:35:43.039 --> 00:35:43.873
Honey.

00:35:44.607 --> 00:35:46.442
These days are different from our time.

00:35:46.909 --> 00:35:49.412
Getting a job at a conglomerate is useless now.

00:35:50.212 --> 00:35:51.681
Just look at you.

00:35:52.348 --> 00:35:54.784
Whether you like it or not,

00:35:54.784 --> 00:35:57.153
a professional career is the only answer.

00:36:05.461 --> 00:36:06.362
Yes.

00:36:08.164 --> 00:36:12.001
My kids shouldn't have to struggle like I did.

00:36:37.927 --> 00:36:38.794
Ji Cheon.

00:36:39.929 --> 00:36:41.063
Help me out.

00:36:57.113 --> 00:36:58.714
You just need me to help you load these, right?

00:36:59.348 --> 00:37:00.616
I can't be late to school today.

00:37:01.617 --> 00:37:02.752
Wait.

00:37:03.285 --> 00:37:05.588
I'll tell them you're quitting your job.

00:37:06.455 --> 00:37:09.125
Come to Seoul with me, okay?

00:37:09.125 --> 00:37:11.227
You said you'd give me a chance.

00:37:11.227 --> 00:37:12.895
You might feel differently after your trip to Seoul.

00:37:12.895 --> 00:37:14.597
How would I feel different?

00:37:17.233 --> 00:37:18.034
Dad.

00:37:19.035 --> 00:37:20.236
I'm not a kid anymore.

00:37:21.203 --> 00:37:22.772
Whatever I do, however I live,

00:37:24.607 --> 00:37:25.574
I'll be the one to decide.

00:37:27.510 --> 00:37:28.678
Go to Seoul by yourself.

00:37:30.312 --> 00:37:31.147
Ji Cheon.

00:37:35.651 --> 00:37:36.552
Seong Ji Cheon.

00:37:39.689 --> 00:37:40.489
Hey.

00:37:41.657 --> 00:37:42.491
Son.

00:37:45.161 --> 00:37:48.230
(Menu of the month)

00:37:56.772 --> 00:37:58.941
He should be here by now. Why isn't he here yet?

00:38:00.009 --> 00:38:01.610
He's not the one to be late.

00:38:02.345 --> 00:38:04.046
Are you waiting for someone?

00:38:04.046 --> 00:38:06.382
I'm not waiting for anyone.

00:38:06.582 --> 00:38:07.483
I'm not.

00:38:07.850 --> 00:38:08.918
If you say so.

00:38:10.753 --> 00:38:12.922
- I'll be in the nutrition room. - Okay.

00:38:14.924 --> 00:38:16.092
Ji Cheon.

00:38:17.293 --> 00:38:18.027
Hi.

00:38:21.263 --> 00:38:23.132
You can't be late without any notice.

00:38:23.866 --> 00:38:25.434
From now on, every morning...

00:38:27.269 --> 00:38:28.771
I mean...

00:38:29.305 --> 00:38:31.374
Text me whenever you come in.

00:38:32.608 --> 00:38:33.509
I will.

00:38:34.543 --> 00:38:35.378
What?

00:38:48.391 --> 00:38:49.425
Ji Cheon.

00:38:50.126 --> 00:38:51.994
Your phone has been ringing for a while now.

00:38:53.763 --> 00:38:55.364
I can answer it later.

00:39:01.871 --> 00:39:02.738
Ji Cheon.

00:39:03.739 --> 00:39:04.774
Come out for a second.

00:39:11.280 --> 00:39:13.816
Come to Seoul with me.

00:39:14.316 --> 00:39:17.420
Let's do everything we can, no matter how it turns out.

00:39:18.320 --> 00:39:19.488
At least pass the board...

00:39:19.488 --> 00:39:21.691
and finish your internship. Then we'll talk, okay?

00:39:22.892 --> 00:39:25.828
So you didn't listen to me at all.

00:39:26.362 --> 00:39:28.497
No. This is all because I believe in you.

00:39:28.497 --> 00:39:30.166
My son, Seong Ji Cheon, can do it.

00:39:30.166 --> 00:39:32.268
You must try everything you can.

00:39:33.169 --> 00:39:34.637
I called you, Dad.

00:39:36.238 --> 00:39:37.006
What?

00:39:40.476 --> 00:39:41.444
To tell you that I was scared.

00:39:42.511 --> 00:39:43.646
That I can't do it.

00:39:46.615 --> 00:39:48.551
But even that day, you didn't answer.

00:39:51.020 --> 00:39:53.022
I didn't?

00:39:53.689 --> 00:39:55.591
When I told you that I didn't want to go to med school, you said,

00:39:55.591 --> 00:39:57.159
"Talk to Mom."

00:39:57.493 --> 00:39:58.995
You just ran away like that.

00:40:00.496 --> 00:40:03.799
Ji Cheon. I did all that for your sake.

00:40:03.799 --> 00:40:05.334
Dad, please! I'm so sick of it.

00:40:07.503 --> 00:40:09.672
You always use us as an excuse, but we're never your priority.

00:40:11.474 --> 00:40:14.377
What exactly did you do for this family?

00:40:33.829 --> 00:40:36.499
(Mat Story)

00:40:55.751 --> 00:40:58.120
Ji Cheon, I...

00:41:43.833 --> 00:41:45.334
Please excuse me.

00:41:58.314 --> 00:42:00.483
This user is not registered.

00:42:00.483 --> 00:42:02.451
Please try again.

00:42:02.451 --> 00:42:03.352
Why won't this work?

00:42:04.186 --> 00:42:05.988
This user is not registered.

00:42:05.988 --> 00:42:07.189
Can I help you?

00:42:07.623 --> 00:42:08.724
Where are you from?

00:42:09.325 --> 00:42:11.927
You must be new here.

00:42:11.927 --> 00:42:13.295
I'm with the New Business...

00:42:14.063 --> 00:42:16.699
I mean, I'm Manager Seong Tae Hun from the Yeonri-ri branch.

00:42:16.699 --> 00:42:17.933
It's been a while since I came to headquarters,

00:42:17.933 --> 00:42:20.636
so my access card isn't working.

00:42:22.038 --> 00:42:24.006
Could you wait here for a moment?

00:42:24.006 --> 00:42:25.041
I'll check on this matter.

00:42:25.508 --> 00:42:27.543
I'm Manager Seong Tae Hun at this company.

00:42:27.543 --> 00:42:29.412
Yes, I understand.

00:42:29.945 --> 00:42:32.715
Please wait here while I verify it.

00:42:33.549 --> 00:42:34.684
All right.

00:42:37.153 --> 00:42:39.188
This user is not registered.

00:42:39.188 --> 00:42:40.556
Please try again.

00:42:41.557 --> 00:42:44.460
Please verify Manager Seong Tae Hun's identity.

00:42:50.299 --> 00:42:52.268
I've submitted the samples,

00:42:52.268 --> 00:42:54.670
and I brought one so you can see it right away.

00:42:54.670 --> 00:42:57.306
I'll begin full-scale cultivation and research it.

00:42:59.475 --> 00:43:01.644
Sir?

00:43:01.644 --> 00:43:03.245
One, two. One, two.

00:43:08.317 --> 00:43:10.486
The executive is really into boxing these days.

00:43:11.687 --> 00:43:12.455
But...

00:43:13.823 --> 00:43:15.891
it's not just about throwing punches.

00:43:15.891 --> 00:43:17.760
Being able to endure the punches. That's what matters most.

00:43:19.128 --> 00:43:20.229
You can hold out a bit longer, right?

00:43:21.163 --> 00:43:21.998
Pardon?

00:43:24.133 --> 00:43:26.602
It's nothing.

00:43:26.602 --> 00:43:28.204
- The sample? - Yes.

00:43:28.204 --> 00:43:29.105
Okay.

00:43:30.072 --> 00:43:31.440
- Right here? - Yes.

00:43:32.308 --> 00:43:33.409
- Here? - Yes.

00:43:45.488 --> 00:43:46.422
Oops.

00:43:46.422 --> 00:43:49.592
I'm sorry. I forgot to take off my gloves.

00:43:51.927 --> 00:43:53.663
Please do a thorough review.

00:43:54.864 --> 00:43:55.731
Sure.

00:43:58.701 --> 00:44:00.236
(Yeonri-ri)

00:44:00.703 --> 00:44:01.737
You're excused.

00:44:03.172 --> 00:44:04.006
Bye.

00:44:13.649 --> 00:44:16.218
It definitely said Yeonri-ri.

00:44:21.123 --> 00:44:24.160
(New Business Department)

00:44:30.533 --> 00:44:31.300
Mr. Seong.

00:44:31.934 --> 00:44:32.735
Hi.

00:44:34.370 --> 00:44:35.404
You're all busy, right?

00:44:37.173 --> 00:44:38.941
Yes, sure.

00:44:39.842 --> 00:44:41.577
- Hey, rookie. - Yes?

00:44:41.577 --> 00:44:43.412
Grab some wet wipes and clean the floor.

00:44:43.412 --> 00:44:44.747
Yes, sir.

00:44:46.882 --> 00:44:50.453
I'm sorry. I came here to submit some seedling samples...

00:44:50.453 --> 00:44:52.621
and stopped by.

00:44:52.621 --> 00:44:54.256
Don't mind me and carry on.

00:44:54.256 --> 00:44:56.392
I'll be heading out soon anyway.

00:44:56.659 --> 00:44:57.560
Mr. Seong.

00:44:59.762 --> 00:45:03.099
If it's okay, could we talk for a bit?

00:45:03.766 --> 00:45:04.667
Talk?

00:45:08.237 --> 00:45:09.071
Okay.

00:45:27.623 --> 00:45:29.125
I guess you don't want to go home today either.

00:45:30.826 --> 00:45:32.695
I'll stay just a little longer.

00:45:32.695 --> 00:45:33.829
Are you getting off work now?

00:45:34.063 --> 00:45:36.365
No, not by myself.

00:45:37.667 --> 00:45:39.068
Let's leave together.

00:45:44.407 --> 00:45:45.441
I'm pretty good, aren't I?

00:45:46.075 --> 00:45:47.009
Be careful.

00:45:48.177 --> 00:45:49.879
Isn't it really pretty here?

00:45:49.879 --> 00:45:50.646
Yes.

00:45:51.480 --> 00:45:53.315
But it's even prettier in there.

00:45:53.315 --> 00:45:55.418
- In there? - Yes, you'll be surprised.

00:46:00.690 --> 00:46:01.757
Are you amazed?

00:46:01.757 --> 00:46:02.558
Yes.

00:46:05.561 --> 00:46:06.629
Look at the lights.

00:46:30.319 --> 00:46:33.189
I hope even more good things come our way in Yeonri-ri.

00:46:33.189 --> 00:46:34.724
The path I really want.

00:46:43.966 --> 00:46:44.800
Here.

00:46:49.939 --> 00:46:51.607
When you're upset,

00:46:51.607 --> 00:46:54.076
you need something sweet and refreshing like this.

00:46:55.311 --> 00:46:56.178
It's good.

00:46:57.046 --> 00:46:59.849
All those messy thoughts disappear after eating something good, right?

00:47:07.490 --> 00:47:08.457
To tell you the truth,

00:47:09.525 --> 00:47:12.828
I saw you arguing with your dad earlier.

00:47:14.196 --> 00:47:15.231
If it's too hard,

00:47:15.231 --> 00:47:17.767
you don't have to force yourself to talk.

00:47:18.200 --> 00:47:21.070
But if you ever want to vent a little?

00:47:21.070 --> 00:47:23.205
Then you can tell me anytime.

00:47:27.843 --> 00:47:28.678
I...

00:47:32.014 --> 00:47:33.215
was scared of the scalpel.

00:47:36.819 --> 00:47:37.953
In an operating room,

00:47:38.854 --> 00:47:41.991
a doctor must hold the scalpel to save people, right?

00:47:42.825 --> 00:47:43.693
But I...

00:47:46.095 --> 00:47:48.297
wasn't sure if I could hold that scalpel for the rest of my life.

00:47:50.700 --> 00:47:52.668
It was a lie when I said I came down here with my dad...

00:47:54.303 --> 00:47:55.271
for a little while.

00:47:56.772 --> 00:47:58.307
I ran away...

00:48:00.376 --> 00:48:01.410
because I wanted to hide.

00:48:08.718 --> 00:48:09.985
Maybe you're not hiding.

00:48:10.786 --> 00:48:12.154
Maybe you're actually moving forward...

00:48:14.490 --> 00:48:16.692
toward a path that truly suits you.

00:48:16.692 --> 00:48:17.760
Slowly...

00:48:18.661 --> 00:48:19.962
At your own pace.

00:48:23.566 --> 00:48:25.735
You don't think it's crazy...

00:48:27.703 --> 00:48:29.205
that I got into med school but dropped out?

00:48:30.406 --> 00:48:33.342
Everybody is a little crazy in a way, right?

00:48:33.342 --> 00:48:34.810
Even my mom says,

00:48:34.810 --> 00:48:37.380
"Have you lost your mind?"

00:48:38.014 --> 00:48:39.015
to me, every day.

00:48:42.551 --> 00:48:44.020
When I'm around you,

00:48:44.653 --> 00:48:48.491
even complicated things start to feel simple.

00:48:48.491 --> 00:48:49.625
That's a good thing, right?

00:48:51.360 --> 00:48:52.628
For me,

00:48:52.628 --> 00:48:56.465
just living with the people I love,

00:48:56.465 --> 00:48:59.368
eating well and sleeping well...

00:48:59.368 --> 00:49:00.603
I think that's the best kind of life.

00:49:01.971 --> 00:49:05.107
That's why I want to live in Yeonri-ri for the rest of my life.

00:49:07.610 --> 00:49:10.479
So I was hoping you get to experience that too,

00:49:12.314 --> 00:49:14.917
but you might go back to Seoul soon.

00:49:17.987 --> 00:49:18.854
Bo Mi.

00:49:20.189 --> 00:49:22.692
Does it bother you that I'm going to Seoul?

00:49:24.026 --> 00:49:25.628
Well...

00:49:26.929 --> 00:49:27.830
Maybe a little?

00:49:29.965 --> 00:49:31.901
Because...

00:49:32.702 --> 00:49:36.138
we'd be short on help. That's all.

00:49:38.808 --> 00:49:39.675
I won't go...

00:49:40.810 --> 00:49:41.777
if you don't want me to.

00:50:06.102 --> 00:50:08.437
Lately, the company's been strangely quiet.

00:50:09.005 --> 00:50:11.173
Projects keep getting cut from the top.

00:50:11.173 --> 00:50:12.641
According to rumors in Human Resources,

00:50:12.641 --> 00:50:15.678
it seems like they're preparing some other major project.

00:50:16.645 --> 00:50:18.547
A major project...

00:50:21.984 --> 00:50:24.020
What you'll be doing in Yeonri-ri...

00:50:24.020 --> 00:50:26.389
is much bigger than you think.

00:50:27.456 --> 00:50:30.126
It's a mission that the future of Mat Story depends on.

00:50:33.729 --> 00:50:34.830
My head is going to explode.

00:50:36.565 --> 00:50:38.601
What else can I do but wait?

00:50:48.010 --> 00:50:48.811
A new phone.

00:50:50.012 --> 00:50:51.447
Okay. Good.

00:50:52.248 --> 00:50:54.884
But it's not the latest model.

00:50:57.253 --> 00:50:58.187
Still, I got a phone.

00:50:58.187 --> 00:50:59.689
Ji Gu, I got you a book.

00:51:00.356 --> 00:51:03.492
I picked it out carefully. I hope you like it.

00:51:04.226 --> 00:51:06.329
The black hole. I love it.

00:51:06.996 --> 00:51:09.398
I've already read it though.

00:51:10.366 --> 00:51:12.335
Even so, thank you.

00:51:12.902 --> 00:51:13.969
You've read it already?

00:51:14.337 --> 00:51:17.006
Dad, can we go to the field this weekend?

00:51:17.306 --> 00:51:19.842
I want to see how much the cabbages have grown.

00:51:20.543 --> 00:51:22.645
Yes, of course.

00:51:23.012 --> 00:51:24.280
Ji Cheon.

00:51:25.047 --> 00:51:26.816
Let's all go together.

00:51:28.818 --> 00:51:30.119
Okay. Let's go.

00:51:33.456 --> 00:51:34.256
By the way,

00:51:34.757 --> 00:51:35.858
there isn't a gift for me?

00:51:36.859 --> 00:51:37.827
What's that?

00:51:38.894 --> 00:51:42.398
This... It's for Ji Cheon.

00:51:43.099 --> 00:51:45.368
I'll buy you something next time.

00:51:45.368 --> 00:51:46.535
Forget it.

00:51:47.436 --> 00:51:49.472
What can I expect from you anyway?

00:52:08.624 --> 00:52:09.525
Hey.

00:52:10.426 --> 00:52:12.595
Give me some time.

00:52:13.829 --> 00:52:17.900
I'll give it serious thought...

00:52:17.900 --> 00:52:19.368
from your perspective.

00:52:24.507 --> 00:52:25.341
Here.

00:52:27.043 --> 00:52:30.913
You used to love it when you were little.

00:52:55.738 --> 00:52:57.106
Do I really have talent for this?

00:53:05.448 --> 00:53:06.482
How amazing.

00:53:12.588 --> 00:53:13.656
What's this?

00:53:20.730 --> 00:53:21.764
Daddy.

00:53:22.665 --> 00:53:23.699
Yes?

00:53:23.699 --> 00:53:26.235
Did you really do all of this by yourself?

00:53:26.902 --> 00:53:29.271
You guys helped Mom dig the rows here.

00:53:29.271 --> 00:53:31.073
Thanks to all of you, I was able to plant them.

00:53:31.073 --> 00:53:33.609
They say our school has a field like this too.

00:53:33.943 --> 00:53:36.178
Do you think I could plant something there someday?

00:53:36.178 --> 00:53:38.381
Yes, of course.

00:53:38.681 --> 00:53:40.583
How's school these days?

00:53:40.583 --> 00:53:42.351
Have you gotten close with your friends?

00:53:42.351 --> 00:53:43.786
I don't have any friends.

00:53:45.021 --> 00:53:48.257
It's because you just sit there reading all day.

00:53:48.257 --> 00:53:49.992
I don't need any friends.

00:53:50.426 --> 00:53:51.327
Sure.

00:53:52.395 --> 00:53:54.230
Friends are really important, you know.

00:53:54.697 --> 00:53:56.298
Why don't we play soccer together sometime?

00:53:56.298 --> 00:53:58.567
Boys usually bond while playing ball.

00:53:58.567 --> 00:54:01.671
But Ji Sang doesn't have friends even if he plays soccer.

00:54:02.605 --> 00:54:04.373
I haven't played soccer once since we got here.

00:54:04.373 --> 00:54:05.341
You don't know what you're talking about.

00:54:06.208 --> 00:54:09.011
Things were going so well. Why are you arguing out of the blue?

00:54:09.779 --> 00:54:12.314
Ji Sang, what was her name again?

00:54:14.750 --> 00:54:16.752
Mary. Have you talked to her?

00:54:17.386 --> 00:54:18.220
Mary...

00:54:19.188 --> 00:54:20.423
It's Carol.

00:54:21.123 --> 00:54:22.758
Why would you bring that up?

00:54:23.626 --> 00:54:25.661
I'm so annoyed.

00:54:25.661 --> 00:54:26.862
I'm sorry, Ji Sang.

00:54:26.862 --> 00:54:27.963
Ji Sang.

00:54:28.731 --> 00:54:29.965
You don't know anything, Dad.

00:54:29.965 --> 00:54:31.767
Ji Gu, where are you going? Ji Sang.

00:54:53.422 --> 00:54:56.892
I've been thinking...

00:54:56.892 --> 00:54:58.361
You don't want me to tell Mom?

00:55:00.062 --> 00:55:01.230
It's not that.

00:55:04.033 --> 00:55:05.835
It must've been agonizing for you.

00:55:08.571 --> 00:55:09.638
I mean it.

00:55:11.407 --> 00:55:13.909
You've always handled things on your own so well...

00:55:14.710 --> 00:55:15.945
so I thought you were okay.

00:55:17.513 --> 00:55:19.081
You must've struggled a lot,

00:55:19.081 --> 00:55:22.418
trying to endure all of our expectations.

00:55:26.122 --> 00:55:28.491
Since coming here, I feel...

00:55:31.260 --> 00:55:32.461
strangely uncomfortable,

00:55:33.329 --> 00:55:34.163
and yet at ease.

00:55:35.898 --> 00:55:38.100
There's nothing but me and the cabbage.

00:55:39.101 --> 00:55:41.470
Since I have time to use my body and breathe...

00:55:42.071 --> 00:55:43.005
I feel like...

00:55:43.906 --> 00:55:46.208
I'm finally seeing things I couldn't see before.

00:55:48.277 --> 00:55:50.546
Did something happen in Seoul?

00:55:51.247 --> 00:55:52.715
No.

00:55:54.383 --> 00:55:56.485
I've lived in Seoul my whole life,

00:55:57.653 --> 00:56:01.090
but maybe because it's been a while?

00:56:02.224 --> 00:56:03.726
It felt suffocating.

00:56:05.127 --> 00:56:07.196
Being able to breathe properly is the most important thing,

00:56:08.197 --> 00:56:11.801
but I wonder if I just didn't realize that before.

00:56:12.768 --> 00:56:14.270
Are you having a tough...

00:56:14.270 --> 00:56:15.338
Let's...

00:56:16.339 --> 00:56:17.673
be honest with Mom too.

00:56:19.342 --> 00:56:20.509
But...

00:56:20.509 --> 00:56:22.978
only once you figure out what you want to do with your life.

00:56:22.978 --> 00:56:26.782
So let's make sure you find what you really want to do.

00:56:29.585 --> 00:56:30.853
You're still young.

00:56:31.487 --> 00:56:33.089
It's not too late, Seong Ji Cheon.

00:56:36.659 --> 00:56:37.693
Ji Gu.

00:56:45.301 --> 00:56:47.470
You're so small.

00:56:47.737 --> 00:56:48.637
What?

00:56:50.072 --> 00:56:53.476
I won't ever give up.

00:56:54.877 --> 00:56:56.178
What's wrong with him?

00:56:56.178 --> 00:56:58.314
The only time I use that word...

00:56:58.314 --> 00:57:00.116
is when I'm sending off fully-grown cabbages to the company.

00:57:00.549 --> 00:57:04.220
In my life, there is no such word as giving up.

00:57:04.220 --> 00:57:06.756
You three and my cabbages.

00:57:08.290 --> 00:57:10.259
Don't touch me.

00:57:14.430 --> 00:57:15.931
Don't come near me.

00:57:16.832 --> 00:57:18.868
(September 24, D-day)

00:57:30.746 --> 00:57:32.481
(Seedling sample submission)

00:57:32.481 --> 00:57:35.851
(D+10)

00:57:39.855 --> 00:57:41.390
(Mat Story, Inbox)

00:57:43.526 --> 00:57:44.427
(Refresh)

00:57:55.371 --> 00:57:57.473
It's been ten days. Why haven't they contacted me?

00:58:09.885 --> 00:58:10.920
Patience.

00:58:13.356 --> 00:58:14.390
Patience.

00:58:30.039 --> 00:58:31.540
You sent the seedlings at least, right?

00:58:32.775 --> 00:58:34.910
Yes, thanks to you telling me about the air holes,

00:58:34.910 --> 00:58:36.178
I safely delivered them.

00:58:37.813 --> 00:58:38.748
Great work.

00:58:39.415 --> 00:58:41.951
Now you can finally stand a little taller, right?

00:58:41.951 --> 00:58:44.220
It must feel rewarding to become like...

00:58:44.220 --> 00:58:45.788
those animals at Mat Story, doesn't it?

00:58:45.788 --> 00:58:47.723
That's a bit harsh, don't you think?

00:58:48.324 --> 00:58:51.127
I'm just doing my best in my position.

00:58:51.727 --> 00:58:52.595
Your best?

00:58:54.196 --> 00:58:56.432
Is exploiting the villagers your best?

00:58:57.333 --> 00:58:58.334
True.

00:58:59.001 --> 00:59:01.337
If you want your sons to recognize you as their father,

00:59:01.337 --> 00:59:02.972
I guess licking Mat Story's boots is the way to go.

00:59:02.972 --> 00:59:04.173
What's a little shame, right?

00:59:04.740 --> 00:59:06.075
What about Mat Story?

00:59:06.976 --> 00:59:11.647
I've never once done anything shameful in front of my kids.

00:59:11.647 --> 00:59:14.917
And for my family, I'd walk straight into hell if I had to.

00:59:16.886 --> 00:59:20.256
You don't even realize you're already standing in hell.

00:59:20.256 --> 00:59:22.024
What an idiot.

00:59:22.024 --> 00:59:23.559
I'm embarrassed for you.

00:59:24.360 --> 00:59:25.728
Why you little...

00:59:55.958 --> 00:59:57.426
- Ji Cheon. - Yes?

00:59:58.861 --> 00:59:59.595
Well...

01:00:00.730 --> 01:00:02.431
What you said before...

01:00:02.431 --> 01:00:04.166
About not going back to Seoul.

01:00:06.168 --> 01:00:07.970
Did you really mean...

01:00:55.151 --> 01:00:57.953
When cabbages grow, caterpillars grow with them.

01:00:58.554 --> 01:01:01.023
As they slowly chew through the leaves,

01:01:01.023 --> 01:01:03.993
they prepare to become butterflies.

01:01:04.994 --> 01:01:07.463
Whether it becomes a war or coexistence...

01:01:07.963 --> 01:01:08.998
No one knows.

01:01:33.589 --> 01:01:36.592
(Cabbage Your Life)

01:01:36.592 --> 01:01:37.860
I haven't even started interfering yet.

01:01:37.860 --> 01:01:40.830
I will tear your whole field apart.

01:01:40.830 --> 01:01:44.033
You really trampled all my precious cabbages?

01:01:44.033 --> 01:01:45.067
Do you have proof?

01:01:45.067 --> 01:01:48.270
There's no reason not to show the security camera footage.

01:01:48.270 --> 01:01:49.739
When a man kisses a woman,

01:01:49.739 --> 01:01:51.807
he should at least follow up on it.

01:01:51.807 --> 01:01:53.242
He hasn't said a word since then.

01:01:53.242 --> 01:01:54.944
Next time, let's go up against each other properly.

01:01:54.944 --> 01:01:55.945
One-on-one.

01:01:55.945 --> 01:01:59.281
Officer Park's the soccer class instructor.

01:01:59.281 --> 01:02:00.216
Isn't he really cool?

01:02:00.916 --> 01:02:04.286
Is it possible that it wasn't the village chief?

